# An `if` whose arm is a bare local moves that local into a binding -- and a
# borrowed parameter cannot move, generic or not. The generic body's arms had
# no type while it was checked, so the move was never judged and the instance
# freed the caller's value (a double free); it is refused as the non-generic
# body is.
pickg: function as { T: AnyRef.generic } in { v: T w: T c: bool } out u64 is {
    r: if c then v else w
    return 0
}

main: function is {
    a: "a".string
    b: "bb".string
    print "\{pickg T: String v: a w: b c: false}"
}
